"id": "3-1",
"t": "VMs and machine families",
"m": 8,
"intro": "Compute Engine gives you virtual machines on Google's infrastructure. You choose a machine family and type (vCPU and memory), a boot image, disks and a network.",
"svc": [
"Compute Engine"
],
"body": "## Machine families\n- **General purpose**: balanced price/performance. E2 (cost-optimized, includes shared-core `e2-micro/small/medium`), N2/N2D/N4, C3/C4 (higher performance), Arm-based options like Tau T2A and C4A (Google Axion).\n- **Compute optimized**: highest per-core performance for HPC, gaming servers, EDA (e.g. C2, H3).\n- **Memory optimized**: very large memory for SAP HANA and in-memory databases (M-series, X4).\n- **Accelerator optimized**: GPUs for ML and graphics (A-series for training/inference, G2 for graphics/inference).\n- **Storage optimized**: high local SSD throughput (Z3).\nNames follow `family-shape-vCPUs`, e.g. `n2-standard-8`, `e2-highmem-4`, `c3-highcpu-22`.\n\n## Custom machine types\nSome families (e.g. E2, N2, N2D) let you choose an exact vCPU/memory combination when predefined shapes waste resources.\n\n## A VM's key settings\nZone, machine type, boot disk image and size, service account, network/subnet, external IP or not, labels and network tags, metadata.\n\n## Pricing model (qualitative)\nBilled per second (after a 1-minute minimum) for vCPU and memory, plus disks, IPs, licenses and network egress. Discounts: sustained use (automatic on some families), committed use (1 or 3 years) and Spot VMs. Stopped VMs don't bill for vCPU/memory but still bill for disks and reserved static IPs.",
"use": "Use Compute Engine for lift-and-shift, custom OS needs, licensed software, stateful legacy apps, or when you need full control (kernel, GPUs, specific CPUs). Prefer Cloud Run or GKE for new stateless containerized services.",
"ex": "A media company runs a Windows-based video transcoder that can't be containerized. It uses `c3-highcpu` VMs for CPU-heavy transcoding and an `e2-standard-2` VM for a small license server.",
"cmd": "gcloud compute machine-types list --zones=us-central1-a --filter=\"name~'^e2'\"\n\ngcloud compute instances create web-1 \\\n  --zone=us-central1-a --machine-type=e2-medium \\\n  --image-family=debian-12 --image-project=debian-cloud \\\n  --boot-disk-size=20GB --tags=http-server \\\n  --service-account=web-sa@shop-dev.iam.gserviceaccount.com --scopes=cloud-platform\n\ngcloud compute instances list\ngcloud compute instances stop web-1 --zone=us-central1-a\ngcloud compute instances set-machine-type web-1 --zone=us-central1-a --machine-type=e2-standard-4",
