"body": "## Editions\n- **Enterprise**: standard managed experience.\n- **Enterprise Plus**: higher performance machine options, a higher availability SLA, data cache and near-zero-downtime maintenance (for supported engines).\n\n## High availability\n**Regional (HA) instance** = primary in one zone + standby in another zone with synchronous replication. Automatic failover if the zone or primary fails; the IP stays the same. The standby can't serve reads.\n\n## Read replicas\nAsynchronous copies for read scaling, in the same or a different region (**cross-region replica**) for DR. A replica can be **promoted** to a standalone primary.\n\n## Backups\nAutomated daily backups + **point-in-time recovery** (using transaction logs). On-demand backups. Restores go to a new or existing instance.\n\n## Connectivity\n- **Private IP** (via Private Services Access or Private Service Connect) or public IP with authorized networks.\n- **Cloud SQL Auth Proxy** / language connectors: IAM-authorized, encrypted connections without managing SSL certs or IP allowlists.\n- **IAM database authentication**: log in with IAM users/SAs instead of passwords (PostgreSQL and MySQL).\n\n## Limits to remember\nStorage can auto-increase (but never decrease). Single primary limits write scaling: scale up, add replicas, or move to AlloyDB/Spanner.",
