"body": "## What makes it special\n- **Relational + SQL** (GoogleSQL or PostgreSQL dialect), schemas, secondary indexes, ACID transactions.\n- **Horizontal scale**: data is split automatically by primary-key ranges across servers. Add compute and both reads and writes scale.\n- **External consistency** across regions, enabled by Google's TrueTime clock infrastructure.\n- **Availability**: multi-region configurations are designed for up to 99.999% availability SLA; regional for up to 99.99%.\n\n## Capacity and editions\nCompute is provisioned in **nodes** or **processing units** (1 node = 1000 PU; you can start smaller than a node). A managed **autoscaler** can adjust capacity. Editions (Standard, Enterprise, Enterprise Plus) unlock features such as multi-region configs and advanced capabilities. Storage is billed separately.\n\n## Schema design\n- **Avoid hotspots**: don't use monotonically increasing primary keys (timestamps, auto-increment). Use UUIDv4, bit-reversed sequences, or hash prefixes.\n- **Interleaved tables** co-locate child rows with parents for fast joins (e.g. `Orders` interleaved in `Customers`).\n- **Change streams** capture data changes for downstream systems.\n- Also supports graph queries (Spanner Graph), full-text search and vector search.",
"use": "Use Spanner for globally distributed OLTP, systems of record that can't tolerate downtime, very high write throughput relational workloads (financial ledgers, inventory, gaming player state). Use Cloud SQL/AlloyDB when a single primary is enough.",
