"body": "## Data model\n- **Table** → rows identified by a single **row key** (the only index) → **column families** → columns (qualifiers) → timestamped cells.\n- Sparse: empty cells take no space. Single-row operations are atomic; no multi-row transactions or joins.\n- Rows are sorted lexicographically by key, so prefix and range scans are fast.\n\n## Architecture\n- **Instance** → one or more **clusters** (in different zones/regions for replication) → **nodes**. Storage is separate (on Colossus), so adding nodes is quick.\n- **App profiles** route traffic: single-cluster routing (strong consistency, transactional single-row ops) or multi-cluster routing (automatic failover, eventual consistency between clusters).\n- SSD or HDD storage; autoscaling of nodes.\n- HBase API compatibility; integrates with Dataflow, Dataproc, BigQuery (external tables).\n\n## Row key design\n- Avoid hotspots: don't start keys with timestamps or sequential IDs.\n- Good pattern: `device#<deviceId>#<reverse_timestamp>` or field promotion like `region#store#date`.\n- Keep keys short; use **Key Visualizer** to find hotspots.",
