"body": "## Data model\n**Collections** contain **documents** (up to 1 MiB each) holding fields, maps and arrays; documents can have **subcollections**. Queries are shallow (per collection or collection group).\n\n## Modes\n- **Native mode**: realtime listeners, mobile/web SDKs, Security Rules, offline support.\n- **Datastore mode**: Datastore API for server apps, no realtime/mobile features.\nA database's mode is chosen at creation. Projects can have multiple Firestore databases. Firestore also offers a MongoDB-compatible API option.\n\n## Indexes and queries\nSingle-field indexes are automatic. Queries combining filters and orderings across fields need **composite indexes** (the error message links to create them). Firestore charges per document read, write and delete, plus storage and network.\n\n## Security\nServer code uses IAM. Client apps (mobile/web) use **Firebase Security Rules** to control which documents each user can access, together with Firebase Authentication.\n\n## Operations\nLocations are regional or multi-regional. Point-in-time recovery, scheduled backups, exports to Cloud Storage, TTL policies to expire documents.",
