"body": "## Roles of projects\n- **Host project**: owns the VPC, subnets, firewall rules, routes, NAT, VPN/Interconnect.\n- **Service projects**: attached to the host; their VMs, GKE clusters, Cloud Run (VPC egress) and other resources use shared subnets.\n- All must be in the **same organization**.\n\n## IAM\n- **Shared VPC Admin** (`roles/compute.xpnAdmin`, at org/folder): enables host projects and attaches service projects.\n- **Network User** (`roles/compute.networkUser`): granted to service project admins/SAs on the whole host project or **specific subnets**, letting them use those subnets.\n- Network admins in the host project manage firewalls and routes centrally.\n\n## Why it matters\nCentral control of IP space, firewalls and hybrid connectivity, with separate billing, quotas and IAM per app project. It's the standard pattern in landing zones.",
