"id": "8-2",
"t": "Cloud CDN and Media CDN",
"m": 6,
"intro": "Cloud CDN caches content at Google's edge locations close to users, in front of the global external Application Load Balancer. Media CDN targets large-scale video and file delivery.",
"svc": [
"Cloud CDN",
"Media CDN"
],
"body": "## How Cloud CDN works\nEnable it on a backend service or backend bucket. Requests hit Google's edge; cache hits are served immediately, misses go to the origin (MIGs, NEGs, Cloud Storage, external origins via internet NEGs).\n\n## Controls\n- **Cache modes**: `CACHE_ALL_STATIC` (default for many setups), `USE_ORIGIN_HEADERS`, `FORCE_CACHE_ALL`.\n- **TTLs**: default, max and client TTLs; negative caching for errors.\n- **Cache keys**: include/exclude protocol, host, query parameters, headers, cookies.\n- **Signed URLs / signed cookies** to restrict premium content.\n- **Invalidation** to purge paths (use versioned file names when possible instead).\n\n## Media CDN\nBuilt on the same infrastructure as YouTube's delivery, optimized for streaming video and large downloads, with its own configuration model (EdgeCacheService) and origin shielding.",
"use": "Use Cloud CDN for websites, APIs with cacheable responses, images and downloads behind the global external Application LB. Use Media CDN for large-scale streaming and gaming downloads.",
