"body": "## Architecture\n- **Storage**: columnar format on Google's distributed file system, replicated within the location. You never manage disks.\n- **Compute**: the Dremel engine executes queries using **slots** (units of CPU/memory/network). Thousands of slots can work on one query.\n- Fast network between them makes separating storage and compute practical.\n\n## Resource model\n`Project → Dataset (has a location) → Tables / views / routines / models`. Jobs (query, load, export, copy) run in a project, which is billed for compute.\n\n## Compute pricing models\n- **On-demand**: pay per TiB of data **scanned** by queries (with a monthly free allowance). Simple, great for spiky or small workloads.\n- **Capacity (Editions)**: Standard, Enterprise and Enterprise Plus editions. Buy **slot reservations** with autoscaling (and optional commitments). Predictable cost for heavy, steady use; editions add features like advanced security and governance.\n\n## Storage pricing\n- **Active** vs **long-term** storage: tables or partitions not modified for 90 consecutive days automatically drop to a lower long-term price.\n- **Logical** (uncompressed) or **physical** (compressed, includes time travel) storage billing per dataset.\n- Batch loading is free; streaming inserts (Storage Write API) are billed.\n\n## Locations\nDatasets are regional (e.g. `us-central1`) or multi-regional (`US`, `EU`). A query can only read datasets in one location.",
"use": "Use BigQuery for analytics, BI, data warehousing, log analysis, ELT and ML on structured/semi-structured data. Not for high-rate single-row OLTP updates (use Cloud SQL/Spanner) or serving low-latency key lookups (use Bigtable/Firestore).",
