"body": "## Ingestion options\n- **Batch load** from Cloud Storage or local files: CSV, JSON (newline-delimited), Avro, Parquet, ORC. Free (uses a shared slot pool). Avro/Parquet carry schemas and load fastest.\n- **Streaming**: the **Storage Write API** (recommended, exactly-once semantics available) or legacy `insertAll`. Pub/Sub **BigQuery subscriptions** write messages directly to tables.\n- **External tables**: query data in Cloud Storage, Bigtable or Google Sheets without loading. **BigLake tables** add fine-grained security and performance features for open formats like Iceberg/Parquet.\n- **Federated queries**: `EXTERNAL_QUERY` against Cloud SQL, AlloyDB or Spanner.\n- **BigQuery Data Transfer Service**: scheduled imports from Google Ads, YouTube, Amazon S3, Redshift, Teradata and more; also scheduled queries.\n\n## SQL features\n- GoogleSQL (standard SQL). Legacy SQL exists but isn't recommended.\n- **Nested and repeated fields** (STRUCT, ARRAY) let you denormalize (e.g. orders with line items) and avoid expensive joins. Use `UNNEST` to flatten.\n- Window functions, geospatial (`GEOGRAPHY`), JSON type, user-defined functions, stored procedures, scripting, `MERGE` for upserts.",
