"id": "9-3",
"t": "Partitioning, clustering and cost control",
"m": 9,
"intro": "Partitioning and clustering let BigQuery skip data it doesn't need, cutting both cost and latency. Combined with guardrails like quotas and maximum bytes billed, they keep the bill under control.",
"svc": [
"BigQuery"
],
"body": "## Partitioning\nDivides a table into segments:\n- **Time-unit column** (DATE/TIMESTAMP/DATETIME by hour, day, month or year).\n- **Ingestion time** (`_PARTITIONTIME`).\n- **Integer range**.\nQueries filtering on the partition column read only matching partitions (**partition pruning**). Options: **require partition filter**, **partition expiration** (auto-delete old partitions).\n\n## Clustering\nSorts data within partitions by up to **four columns** (e.g. `customer_id, country`). Filters and aggregations on clustered columns read fewer blocks. BigQuery re-clusters automatically in the background at no cost. Works on non-partitioned tables too.\n\n## Which to use\n- High-cardinality filter columns → clustering.\n- Time-based filtering, lifecycle management, or the need for precise cost estimates → partitioning.\n- Both together is common: partition by `event_date`, cluster by `user_id`.\n\n## Other cost controls\n- Select only needed columns; preview tables instead of `SELECT *`.\n- `--maximum_bytes_billed` on queries; **custom quotas** (query usage per day per project or user).\n- Materialized views and BI Engine for repeated dashboard queries.\n- Monitor with `INFORMATION_SCHEMA.JOBS` (bytes billed by user/query).",
"use": "Partition large fact tables by date and require a partition filter. Cluster on the columns most used in WHERE and JOIN. Add custom quotas in projects where analysts experiment.",
"ex": "An events table of several TB per day is partitioned by `DATE(event_ts)` with 400-day expiration and clustered by `customer_id, event_name`. A dashboard querying one week for one customer scans a tiny fraction of what it did before.",
"cmd": "bq query --use_legacy_sql=false '\nCREATE TABLE analytics.events\nPARTITION BY DATE(event_ts)\nCLUSTER BY customer_id, event_name\nOPTIONS (require_partition_filter = TRUE, partition_expiration_days = 400)\nAS SELECT * FROM analytics.events_raw'\n\nbq query --use_legacy_sql=false '\nSELECT user_email, SUM(total_bytes_billed)/POW(1024,4) AS tib\nFROM `region-us`.INFORMATION_SCHEMA.JOBS\nWHERE creation_time > TIMESTAMP_SUB(CURRENT_TIMESTAMP(), INTERVAL 30 DAY)\nGROUP BY user_email ORDER BY tib DESC'",
