"body": "## Cloud Composer\n- Managed **Apache Airflow**. Pipelines are **DAGs** written in Python, stored in the environment's Cloud Storage bucket.\n- Rich operators for BigQuery, Dataflow, Dataproc, Cloud Storage, Kubernetes, external systems; retries, SLAs, backfills, sensors.\n- Composer runs on Google-managed infrastructure (latest generations abstract away the underlying GKE cluster). It has a baseline cost even when idle.\n- Lighter alternatives: **Workflows** (serverless), **Cloud Scheduler**, Dataform schedules.\n\n## Dataform\n- Develop **SQLX** files (SQL + config) with dependencies via `ref()`, **assertions** (data quality tests), incremental tables, documentation, Git integration.\n- Compiles to a dependency graph and runs in BigQuery. Built into BigQuery Studio; schedule with workflow configurations.\n- The Google Cloud equivalent of the \"analytics engineering\" approach popularized by tools like dbt.\n\n## Datastream\nServerless **change data capture (CDC)** from MySQL, PostgreSQL, Oracle, SQL Server (and more) to BigQuery (direct) or Cloud Storage. Low-latency replication for analytics without hammering the source.",
