"t": "The AI/ML landscape on Google Cloud",
"m": 7,
"intro": "Google Cloud offers AI at every level: ready-made APIs, generative models (Gemini) via Vertex AI, AutoML for custom models without much code, full custom training, and ML inside BigQuery.",
"svc": [
"Vertex AI",
"Cloud Vision API",
"Speech-to-Text",
"Document AI",
"Translation API"
],
"body": "## Pick the lowest level of effort that works\n1. **Pre-trained APIs**: no ML expertise needed. Vision (labels, OCR), Video Intelligence, Speech-to-Text, Text-to-Speech, Translation, Natural Language, **Document AI** (invoices, forms, IDs).\n2. **Generative AI on Vertex AI**: Gemini models (text, code, image, audio, video understanding), Imagen (images), Veo (video), Chirp (speech), plus partner and open models in **Model Garden**. Prompt, ground, tune.\n3. **AutoML**: train custom models on your labeled data (tabular, image, video) with minimal code.\n4. **Custom training**: your own code (TensorFlow, PyTorch, JAX, scikit-learn, XGBoost) on managed infrastructure with GPUs/TPUs.\n5. **BigQuery ML**: SQL-based models where the data lives.\n\n## Vertex AI = the unified ML platform\nDatasets, Workbench and Colab Enterprise notebooks, training, Model Registry, endpoints, batch prediction, pipelines, Feature Store, model monitoring, Vertex AI Studio, Agent Builder, evaluation.\n\n## Gemini for Google Cloud\nSeparate from building with models: **Gemini Code Assist** and Gemini in the Console/BigQuery help *you* write code, SQL and troubleshoot.\n\n## Data governance\nGoogle states that customer data sent to Vertex AI generative models isn't used to train Google's foundation models without permission. Check the current data governance docs for specifics.",
"use": "Start with a pre-trained API or a Gemini prompt; move to AutoML or tuning only if quality isn't enough; build custom training only when you need full control. Keep simple predictive analytics in BigQuery ML.",
"ex": "An insurer processes claim forms with Document AI (pre-trained form parser), summarizes adjuster notes with Gemini on Vertex AI, and predicts fraud with a custom XGBoost model trained on Vertex AI, while analysts forecast claim volume with BigQuery ML.",
"cmd": "gcloud services enable aiplatform.googleapis.com vision.googleapis.com documentai.googleapis.com\n\n# Label detection with the Vision API\ngcloud ml vision detect-labels gs://cloud-samples-data/vision/label/wakeupcat.jpg\n\n# Translate text\ncurl -s -X POST -H \"Authorization: Bearer $(gcloud auth print-access-token)\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  \"https://translation.googleapis.com/v3/projects/kav-gcp-lab:translateText\" \\\n  -d '{\"contents\":[\"Hello, cloud!\"],\"targetLanguageCode\":\"es\"}'",
"gotchas": [
"Pre-trained APIs are billed per unit (images, characters, minutes, pages); estimate volumes first.",
"Generative model availability varies by region; some models are only in certain locations or the global endpoint.",
"AutoML and custom models need good labeled data; garbage in, garbage out."
],
