"id": "12-6",
"t": "Fleet visibility: Asset Inventory, Active Assist, quotas and support",
"m": 6,
"intro": "Operating at scale means knowing what you have (Cloud Asset Inventory), acting on recommendations (Active Assist), watching quotas and Google Cloud service health, and knowing how to get support.",
"svc": [
"Cloud Asset Inventory",
"Active Assist",
"Personalized Service Health",
"Cloud Quotas"
],
"body": "## Cloud Asset Inventory\nSearch and export all resources and IAM policies across the org (current and historical metadata). Answer questions like \"all public buckets\", \"VMs with external IPs\", \"who has Owner anywhere\". Real-time feeds to Pub/Sub on changes. Powers Policy Analyzer.\n\n## Active Assist (Recommender)\nRecommendations for **cost** (idle VMs, rightsizing, unattached disks, idle IPs, CUD purchases), **security** (excess IAM permissions), **performance** and **reliability**, and **sustainability** (carbon footprint). Use them via the Console, API or BigQuery export.\n\n## Quotas\n**Cloud Quotas** shows quota usage and limits; set quota alerts and request increases in advance of launches. Quotas are per project (some per region).\n\n## Service health and support\n- **Personalized Service Health**: Google Cloud incidents relevant to your projects, with alerts.\n- **Customer Care** support offerings range from basic (billing) to Standard, Enhanced and Premium (response times, technical account management). Check current plans.",
"use": "Use Asset Inventory for audits and automation, Active Assist weekly for cost and security cleanup, quota monitoring before launches, and Personalized Service Health in incident runbooks.",
