"body": "## What it covers (paraphrased)\n- **Digital transformation**: why cloud (agility, scale, OpEx vs CapEx), cloud models, shared responsibility.\n- **Data**: data's value, databases vs warehouses vs data lakes, BigQuery, Looker, streaming with Pub/Sub/Dataflow.\n- **AI/ML**: pre-trained APIs vs AutoML vs custom, generative AI with Gemini and Vertex AI, responsible AI.\n- **Infrastructure and app modernization**: VMs, containers, serverless, hybrid/multicloud (GKE Enterprise), APIs (Apigee), migration approaches.\n- **Trust and security**: defense in depth, zero trust, IAM, encryption, compliance, resource hierarchy.\n- **Operations**: reliability/SRE ideas, cost management (budgets, CUDs), support options, sustainability.\n\n## High-yield distinctions\n- CapEx (buy upfront) vs **OpEx** (pay as you go) and TCO.\n- IaaS vs PaaS vs SaaS vs serverless, with a Google example of each.\n- Data warehouse (BigQuery) vs operational database (Cloud SQL/Spanner) vs data lake (Cloud Storage).\n- Pre-trained API → AutoML → custom model → generative AI.\n- Rehost vs replatform vs refactor.\n- Google's network, regions and zones, and why multi-zone matters.\n\n## How to study here\nLessons in Levels 0, 1, 2, 9, 10, 13, 14 plus the CDL practice set in Practice.",
"use": "Take CDL if you're new to cloud, in a business/technical sales/PM role, or want a first milestone before ACE. Engineers can still benefit as a warm-up but may jump straight to ACE.",
