"body": "## Areas (paraphrased)\n- **Setting up an environment**: projects, folders, billing accounts and budgets, enabling APIs, installing/configuring gcloud, Cloud Identity basics.\n- **Planning and implementing**: choosing and deploying Compute Engine, GKE, Cloud Run, Cloud Run functions, App Engine; storage and database options; VPCs, subnets, firewall rules, load balancers, Cloud VPN; deploying with IaC (Terraform, Infrastructure Manager).\n- **Ensuring successful operation**: managing VMs and MIGs, GKE operations (node pools, scaling, kubectl), Cloud Run revisions/traffic, snapshots/images, Cloud Storage lifecycle, Monitoring/Logging, log sinks, alerting.\n- **Configuring access and security**: IAM roles (basic vs predefined vs custom), service accounts and impersonation, audit logs, Org Policy basics.\n\n## Commands worth knowing cold\n- `gcloud config set project|compute/region|compute/zone`, `gcloud config configurations create/activate`\n- `gcloud compute instances create … --machine-type --image-family --tags --service-account --scopes`\n- `gcloud compute instance-groups managed create/set-autoscaling/rolling-action start-update`\n- `gcloud container clusters create(-auto)/get-credentials`, `kubectl apply/get/scale/rollout`\n- `gcloud run deploy … --region --allow-unauthenticated`, `update-traffic`\n- `gcloud storage buckets create/cp/rsync`, `gcloud storage buckets update --lifecycle-file`\n- `gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding`, `gcloud iam service-accounts create/keys`, `--impersonate-service-account`\n- `bq mk/query/load`, `gcloud sql instances create`, `gcloud logging sinks create`\n\n## High-yield traps\n- Basic roles are rarely the right answer; predefined roles are.\n- Billing: Billing Account User links projects; budgets don't cap spend.\n- Stopping a VM doesn't stop disk billing.\n- To change a MIG, create a new template.",
