"body": "## Areas (paraphrased)\n- Designing and planning a solution architecture (business + technical requirements, network/storage/compute choices, migration planning).\n- Managing and provisioning infrastructure (network topologies, storage systems, compute, IaC).\n- Designing for security and compliance (IAM, data protection, VPC SC, compliance regimes).\n- Analyzing and optimizing technical and business processes (SDLC, CI/CD, cost, stakeholder management, DR testing).\n- Managing implementation (working with teams, migration execution, APIs, testing).\n- Ensuring solution and operations reliability (monitoring, SLOs, incident and release management).\n\n## Case studies\nThe exam includes questions about **published case studies** (fictional companies with business and technical requirements). Read the current ones on the official exam page before your test, map their requirements to services, and practice with the case studies in this app's Cases tab.\n\n## How architects think in this exam\n1. Find the **hard requirements** (compliance, RTO/RPO, latency, global users, existing tech).\n2. Eliminate options that violate any requirement.\n3. Among the rest, prefer **managed/serverless**, **least operational overhead**, **least privilege**, and **cost-effective** solutions.\n4. Watch for keywords: \"global consistency\" → Spanner; \"streaming with windowing\" → Dataflow; \"existing Hadoop\" → Dataproc; \"no code changes VMware\" → VMware Engine; \"exfiltration\" → VPC SC; \"keys outside Google\" → EKM; \"UDP\" → passthrough NLB.\n\n## Design checklist\nIdentity & hierarchy → network → compute → data → security controls → observability/SLOs → DR → cost → migration path.",
"use": "Take PCA after ACE-level hands-on experience and once you're comfortable with every level in this curriculum. The case studies here mirror the reasoning the exam expects.",
"ex": "For a case like \"a global game studio needs low-latency matchmaking and a consistent player inventory worldwide\", the architect picks GKE or Cloud Run regionally near players, Spanner multi-region for inventory, Memorystore for sessions, Pub/Sub + Dataflow + BigQuery for analytics, global LB with Cloud Armor.",
