"body": "## Question anatomy\nA short scenario, a goal (\"what should you do?\") and qualifiers: **most cost-effective**, **least operational overhead**, **Google-recommended**, **minimize changes**, **most secure**. The qualifier decides between otherwise valid answers.\n\n## Elimination process\n1. Underline the qualifier and hard constraints.\n2. Remove options that don't solve the problem.\n3. Remove options that violate a constraint (region, compliance, budget, \"no code changes\").\n4. Of what's left, pick the most managed, least-privilege, Google-recommended choice.\n\n## Recurring patterns\n- \"Give access to a group of users\" → Google group + predefined role.\n- \"App on Compute Engine needs to call an API\" → attached service account, not keys.\n- \"Temporary access\" → IAM Conditions.\n- \"Reduce cost for fault-tolerant batch\" → Spot VMs.\n- \"Archive rarely accessed data\" → Archive/Coldline + lifecycle.\n- \"Analytics on huge data with SQL\" → BigQuery.\n- \"Event-driven processing of uploaded files\" → Cloud Storage + Eventarc + Cloud Run functions.\n- \"Private VMs need internet updates\" → Cloud NAT.\n- \"SSH without public IP\" → IAP TCP forwarding.\n\n## Logistics\nExams are taken online-proctored or at test centers; review the current exam guide, duration and policies on the official certification site. Flag hard questions and return; never leave one blank.",
"use": "Use the Practice tab's exam sets, then review every miss via its linked lesson. Track your weakest levels in Progress.",
