"flow": "1. Clinics send HL7v2 messages and FHIR bundles into Healthcare API stores inside a VPC Service Controls perimeter.\n2. FHIR changes stream into a PHI BigQuery dataset for operational analytics; clinicians use a FHIR-based app protected by IAP.\n3. The Healthcare API de-identify operation writes a de-identified copy of the dataset, which is exported into a separate research project.\n4. Sensitive Data Protection scans free-text fields and files to catch PHI that structured de-identification missed.\n5. Audit logs for every PHI read land in a central, access-restricted log project.",
"trade": "| Choice | Benefit | Cost / risk |\n|---|---|---|\n| Healthcare API vs custom FHIR server on GKE | Managed, standards-based, de-id built in | Less flexibility for non-standard extensions |\n| Separate research project | Clean blast-radius boundary for PHI | Data copies to keep in sync; storage cost |\n| VPC Service Controls | Exfiltration protection | Complex for third-party integrations; plan bridges and access levels |\n| Data Access logs | Strong audit story | Volume and cost |",
"exam": "Compliance on Google Cloud is shared responsibility: Google offers a BAA and compliant infrastructure, but the customer must configure services correctly and only put PHI in covered services. \"FHIR / HL7\" → Cloud Healthcare API. \"Find and mask sensitive data\" → Sensitive Data Protection.",
