"flow": "1. Sensors publish over MQTT to brokers at the edge; a bridge forwards messages to Pub/Sub, buffering locally if the plant loses connectivity.\n2. Dataflow reads Pub/Sub, de-duplicates, computes per-machine windows, and flags anomalies; alerts go out within seconds.\n3. Latest readings and recent series go to Bigtable for dashboards; all data streams into partitioned BigQuery tables.\n4. Raw messages are archived in Cloud Storage for low-cost retention.\n5. Data scientists train failure-prediction models in BigQuery ML or Vertex AI and deploy predictions back into the pipeline.",
"trade": "| Choice | Benefit | Cost / risk |\n|---|---|---|\n| Bigtable for serving time series | Millisecond reads at huge write rates | Row key design is critical; minimum node cost even when idle |\n| BigQuery for history | Serverless SQL over years of data | Streaming ingestion and scan costs; partition and cluster tables |\n| Dataflow streaming | Exactly-once processing semantics, autoscaling | Pipeline cost runs 24/7; tune workers |\n| Partner or self-managed MQTT | Replaces retired IoT Core | Another component to secure and operate |",
"exam": "IoT Core is retired: answer with MQTT broker + Pub/Sub. \"Time series, high write throughput, low-latency key lookups\" → Bigtable. \"Stream processing with windows\" → Dataflow. Avoid sequential row keys in Bigtable (hotspotting).",
"q": [
[
"FactoryPulse previously used Cloud IoT Core. What replaces it in a current design?",
[
"Cloud IoT Core v2 device registries",
"An MQTT broker forwarding device messages to Pub/Sub",
"Firebase Cloud Messaging topics per device",
"Cloud Tasks queues with one task per reading"
],
1,
"Cloud IoT Core was retired in August 2023; Google recommends partner MQTT solutions feeding Pub/Sub."
],
[
"Which database best serves \"latest reading for machine X\" at tens of thousands of writes per second?",
[
"Cloud SQL for MySQL",
"Bigtable with a row key like machineId#reversedTimestamp",
"BigQuery with streaming inserts",
"Firestore with a document per reading"
],
1,
"Bigtable handles very high write throughput with low-latency key lookups; a reversed timestamp puts the newest row first."
],
[
"Why is a Bigtable row key that starts with the timestamp a poor choice here?",
[
"Bigtable rejects row keys that begin with numbers",
"Current writes all land on one tablet (a hotspot)",
"Timestamp-first keys double the storage cost",
"Timestamp-first keys disable cluster replication"
],
1,
"Sequential keys concentrate writes in one key range; leading with machine ID spreads load."
],
[
"Which service performs windowed aggregation and anomaly detection on the streaming data?",
[
"Cloud Scheduler",
"Dataflow",
"Cloud Composer",
"Transfer Appliance"
],
1,
"Dataflow (Apache Beam) supports streaming windows, triggers and stateful processing."
]
]
